@file sybase-cdc-connector/src/test/java/com/phoenix/cdc/sybase/cdc/TransactionBufferTest.java
@summary
<p><b>Role:</b> unit test for <a href="TransactionBuffer.html">TransactionBuffer</a>: two interleaved transactions, one rolled back and one committed. Proves "publish only on COMMIT, in log order, discard on ROLLBACK" without a database.</p>
@@ 1
<p>Same package as the class under test.</p>
@@ 3-5
<p>Imports the command record and its enum, and JUnit.</p>
@@ 7-9
<p>JDK types.</p>
@@ 11-12
<p>Static assertion imports.</p>
@@ 14
<p>Test class.</p>
@@ 16-19
<p>Helper building a fake command: the transaction id and OQID are single bytes; INSERT commands get an after image <code>{id: oqid}</code> so the test can check which rows were released.</p>
@@ 21-22
<p>The test method.</p>
@@ 23-29
<p>Feed: BEGIN 1, BEGIN 2, INSERT in 1, INSERT in 2 (interleaved, as in a real log), INSERT in 1, ROLLBACK 2. Nothing is released yet.</p>
@@ 30-31
<p>COMMIT 1 releases a transaction.</p>
@@ 32
<p>It contains exactly transaction 1's rows (ids 3 and 5) in log order; transaction 2's row (id 4) is gone.</p>
@@ 33
<p>No transactions remain open.</p>
@@ 34-35
<p>End of test and class.</p>
